\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related_work}

\paragraph{ViT token pruning.}
DynamicViT~\cite{rao2021dynamicvit}, EViT~\cite{liang2022evit}, A-ViT~\cite{yin2022avit}, and Token Merging~\cite{bolya2023tome} remove 50--66\% of tokens with under 0.5\,pp ImageNet accuracy loss. Their success rests on classification's insensitivity to spatial layout; robotic manipulation inverts this assumption, as grasping depends on spatial arrangement. None has been evaluated in closed-loop VLA control.

\paragraph{Token efficiency in VLMs and VLAs.}
FastV~\cite{chen2024fastv} and PruMerge~\cite{shang2024prumerge} reduce vision tokens in VLMs using language-backbone attention signals. ``Don't Run with Scissors''~\cite{jabbour2025dontrun} analyzes VLM token pruning for visual question answering; our work targets closed-loop robotic manipulation, where pruning failures directly impact physical task execution rather than text generation quality. VLA-specific methods have emerged in parallel: VLA-IAP~\cite{cheng2026vlaiap} aligns pruning with action-prediction importance, VLA-Cache~\cite{xu2025vlacache} compresses at the KV-cache level, EfficientVLA~\cite{yang2025efficientvla} combines pruning with merging, and VLA-Pruner~\cite{liu2025vlapruner} learns a pruning policy jointly with the action head. LightVLA~\cite{jiang2026lightvla} introduces differentiable pruning and Compressor-VLA~\cite{gao2025compressorvla} applies instruction-guided compression, both targeting individual architectures; our work instead asks how architectural choices determine which compression approaches succeed or fail, finding that scoring validity is architecture-dependent; L2 norm selection is anti-informative on entangling connectors while attention scoring recovers near-baseline performance.

\paragraph{Vision connectors.}
The connector between ViT and language backbone governs how spatial information distributes across tokens. LLaVA~\cite{liu2023llava} projects patches independently through an MLP; BLIP-2~\cite{li2023blip2} uses cross-attention queries (structurally similar to our VTR re-encoder); pixel shuffle~\cite{shi2016subpixel} folds spatial neighborhoods into channels, adopted by SmolVLA~\cite{shukor2025smolvla}. These create qualitatively different token dependencies; independent connectors leave patch information separable, while entangling connectors distribute content across tokens. The pruning consequences have not been characterized.

We provide the first cross-architecture analysis of how connector coupling and task complexity jointly govern VLA token compressibility, introducing CV of token norms as a single-pass diagnostic that correlates with compressibility without closed-loop evaluation.

