\section{VTR Training Details}
\label{app:smart_compress_details}

The VTR module is a cross-attention pooling layer inserted between SmolVLA's pixel-shuffle vision connector and the Qwen2-0.5B language backbone. It consists of $M$ learned query vectors that attend over the 128 vision tokens through standard multi-head cross-attention, producing $M$ compressed tokens as input to the LLM. The compressor adds 22.2M trainable parameters (approximately 5\% of SmolVLA's 451.5M total). Training is end-to-end: compressor and VLA policy parameters are jointly optimized.

